Z||000000||SLYGUY||09-08-2001||09:16 PM||||My cruise doesn't work on my fiero. I can't find a fuse for it. What is the most common ailment for this? I'm going to order the book from the fierostore made just for that, but anyone have any ideas to start me off?<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=SLYGUY&album_id=35876&image_id=7&courtesy=1"> <P>88GT <BR>all stock...||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||09-08-2001||09:20 PM||||Check all of the vacuum lines.  I think the most common failure is the signal stalk.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-08-2001||11:37 PM||||Sly,,, two things.... please trim that image down and then use PIP to put it on a forum server. (Image Poster is on the bottom of the page.) We all get enough spam without PrintRoom's image tags and cookies.... PIP is free and won't tag your photo's.<P>First thing to check is all the vacuum plumbing and the nasty vacuum reserve can. it just loves to rust.<P>Next check the stalk. <P>If it's a stick check the switch on the clutch. the one with thin wires.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||09-09-2001||01:29 AM||||Thanks ogre...<P>I'll look into that.<P>Sly||||reg||1
